window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-7f6cc4f4846d0d0d"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"automate-security-scans-in-ci\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"ci\">在 CI 中自动运行安全扫描</h1> <p>扫描拉取请求、合并到主分支的提交，或按计划扫描整个代码库。</p> <p>将 Codex Security CLI 接入 CI 流程。选择扫描时机和代码范围，保留发现项与覆盖情况，并决定扫描结果如何影响交付。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>希望在拉取请求或合并请求中加入安全检查的团队。</li> <li>希望在更改合入默认分支后扫描该分支的维护者。</li> <li>需要定期评估代码库的安全团队。 <a id=\"related-links\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_2\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">在 CI 中运行 Codex Security</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0c31a6fce966b88c\">在 GitLab CI/CD 中运行 Codex Security</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在桌面应用中审查代码更改（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>将安全扫描纳入开发流程。你可以在拉取请求中扫描、在更改合入默认分支后扫描，或按固定周期扫描。根据触发条件选择适当的扫描范围，保留发现项和覆盖情况，并为团队建立可重复的结果审查流程。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-when-to-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">选择扫描时机</h2> <p>先选择一个符合团队工作方式的触发条件。了解扫描耗时、成本以及团队如何使用发现项后，再逐步增加其他触发方式。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>运行时机</th> <th>建议范围</th> <th>有助于审查的内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>按计划运行</td> <td>整个代码库，可选择深度扫描</td> <td>定期检查更广泛的代码库。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>向 main 分支提交时</td> <td>推送提交中的整个代码库</td> <td>更改合入默认分支后的集成代码。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>拉取请求或合并请求中</td> <td>合并基点与拟合并提交之间的更改</td> <td>在合并前发现潜在的安全回归。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>如果仓库的默认分支名称不是 <code>main</code>，请使用实际的分支名。要同时配置触发条件和扫描范围：拉取请求差异扫描只覆盖该次更改，不会扫描整个代码库。在更改合入 <code>main</code> 后才运行的扫描，无法阻止已经合并的拉取请求。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">开始之前</h2> <p>你需要有权评估目标代码库、有权配置其 CI 流程与机密信息，并拥有可使用 Codex Security 的 OpenAI API 密钥。请参阅 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CLI 快速入门（本地尚未收录）</a>，确认访问权限和设置要求。</p> <p>请使用符合 <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci#prepare-the-workflow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CI 要求</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>的可信运行器。扫描会使用运行器在本地拥有的权限。不要把无关凭据放进扫描作业，并遵守平台针对来自分叉仓库的拉取请求和其他不可信代码所设的限制。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-your-pipeline\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">设置流水线</h2> <ol> <li>在流水线中加入 Codex Security</li> </ol> <p>选择适合你所用 CI 平台的示例。按照示例安装 Codex Security CLI，并通过 CI 提供商的机密存储提供 API 密钥。</p> <p>选择一个起点：</p> <ul> <li><strong>GitHub Actions：</strong>使用<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci#add-the-github-actions-workflow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">拉取请求工作流</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>扫描拟议更改并保留结果。</li> <li><strong>GitLab CI/CD：</strong>按照<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci/gitlab\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">流水线指南（本地尚未收录）</a>设置合并请求、默认分支扫描和计划扫描。指南包含可下载的流水线示例，并说明应启用哪些选项。</li> <li> <p><strong>其他 CI 平台：</strong>根据你的提供商，调整<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">在 CI 中运行 Codex Security（本地尚未收录）</a>中的扫描和导出命令，包括触发条件、机密存储、检出和制品处理方式。</p> </li> <li> <p>配置触发条件和范围</p> </li> </ul> <p>更改合入 <code>main</code> 后，在推送的提交上扫描整个仓库；同时为所选分支安排周期扫描。每周扫描是不错的起点，可根据仓库活动、扫描时长和费用调整频率。</p> <p>对于拉取请求或合并请求，请获取基分支和头分支的提交历史，并扫描二者合并基点之后的已提交差异。</p> <p>配置每个作业，让它扫描预期的代码：定期扫描和 <code>main</code> 分支提交应覆盖整个仓库，拉取请求则应覆盖拟议更改。按照平台示例设置适当的扫描范围。</p> <p>根据扫描范围和频率设定预算。扫描整个仓库可能比差异扫描耗时更长、成本更高。请将 <code>--max-cost</code> 视为估算成本限制，而不是硬性支出上限。达到该值时，扫描覆盖范围可能仍不完整。</p> <ol> <li>运行流水线并审查结果</li> </ol> <p>按照常规审查流程提交流水线更改，然后触发扫描。在运行结果和 <code>scan-manifest.json</code> 中确认目标修订版本和扫描范围。</p> <p>查看已保存报告中的发现项和支持证据。即使扫描没有报告发现项，也要检查 <code>coverage.json</code> 中是否有未完成或延后的区域。在提高频率或扩展到更多仓库之前，先审查运行时间和成本。</p> <p>将报告作为 CI 制品保留。根据源代码和证据的敏感程度设置合适的制品访问权限和保留期限。</p> <p>你还可以选择导出 SARIF（一种结构化安全发现格式），在平台的安全界面中显示结果。有关支持的版本、权限和许可要求，请查看相应的平台指南。</p> <ol> <li>决定是否让发现项阻止合并</li> </ol> <p>一开始先审查发现项，但暂不阻止合并。团队熟悉结果后，可以要求拉取请求必须通过安全检查，例如在扫描发现高危或严重等级的漏洞时阻止合并。</p> <p>始终确认扫描是否完成，以及它覆盖了哪些代码。即使扫描没有报告发现项，失败的扫描或被跳过的代码仍需要处理。</p> <p>有关设置详情，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci#choose-a-severity-policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">配置严重性阈值并解读扫描结果</a>（官网章节，需联网） <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">本地页面（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <ol> <li>跟进发现项</li> </ol> <p>按照团队的常规流程分派发现项，以便调查或修复。提供已扫描的提交、受影响代码和支持证据，方便其他开发者继续调查。</p> <p>关闭发现项之前先验证修复；对于覆盖不完整的部分，应安排后续扫描。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"automate-security-scans-in-ci\">Automate security scans in CI</h1> <p>Scan pull requests, commits to main, or your repository on a schedule.</p> <p>Add the Codex Security CLI to your CI pipeline. Choose when to scan and which code to review, preserve findings and coverage, and decide how results should affect delivery.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Teams adding security checks to pull or merge requests.</li> <li>Maintainers scanning their default branch after changes land.</li> <li>Security teams scheduling recurring repository assessments.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8d926b82884d5f99\">Run Codex Security in CI</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0c31a6fce966b88c\">Run Codex Security in GitLab CI/CD</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/scan-code-changes-for-security\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Review code changes in the desktop app (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Make security scanning part of your development workflow. Run Codex Security on pull requests, after changes reach your default branch, or on a recurring schedule. Choose the scan scope that fits each trigger, preserve findings and coverage, and give your team a repeatable way to review the results.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-when-to-scan\">Choose when to scan</h2> <p>Start with one trigger that fits your team's workflow. Add others as you learn how long scans take, what they cost, and how your team uses the findings.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>When to run</th> <th>Suggested scope</th> <th>What it helps you review</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>On a schedule</td> <td>Full repository, optionally using a deep scan</td> <td>The broader codebase at a recurring interval.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>On commits to main</td> <td>Full repository at the pushed commit</td> <td>The integrated code after changes reach your default branch.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>On pull or merge requests</td> <td>Changes between the merge base and proposed commit</td> <td>Potential security regressions before merge.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Use your repository's default branch if it has a name other than <code>main</code>. Configure both the trigger and the scan scope: a pull-request diff scan covers that change, not the entire repository. A scan after changes reach <code>main</code> cannot block a pull request that has already merged.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>You'll need a repository you're authorized to assess, permission to configure its CI pipeline and secrets, and an OpenAI API key with Codex Security access. Use the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CLI quickstart (not in this local snapshot)</a> to check access and setup requirements.</p> <p>Use a trusted runner that meets the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci#prepare-the-workflow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CI requirements</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a>. Scans run with the runner's local permissions. Keep unrelated credentials out of the scan job, and follow your platform's restrictions for pull requests from forks and other untrusted code.</p> <h2 id=\"set-up-your-pipeline\">Set up your pipeline</h2> <ol> <li>Add Codex Security to your pipeline</li> </ol> <p>Choose the example for your CI platform. Follow it to install the Codex Security CLI and provide an API key through your CI provider's secret store.</p> <p>Choose a starting point: - <strong>GitHub Actions:</strong> Use the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci#add-the-github-actions-workflow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">pull-request workflow</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a> to scan proposed changes and preserve results. - <strong>GitLab CI/CD:</strong> Use the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci/gitlab\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">pipeline guide (not in this local snapshot)</a> for merge requests, default-branch scans, and scheduled scans. It includes a downloadable pipeline and explains which options to enable. - <strong>Other CI platforms:</strong> Adapt the scan and export commands in <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Run Codex Security in CI (not in this local snapshot)</a> to your provider's triggers, secret store, checkout, and artifact handling.</p> <ol> <li>Configure the trigger and scope</li> </ol> <p>Scan the repository at the pushed commit when changes reach <code>main</code>, and on a recurring schedule for your chosen branch. Weekly scans are a good place to start; adjust the cadence based on repository activity, scan duration, and cost.</p> <p>For pull or merge requests, fetch the base and head history and scan the committed diff from their merge base.</p> <p>Configure each job to scan the intended code: the full repository for scheduled scans and commits to <code>main</code>, or the proposed changes for pull requests. Follow your platform's example to set up the appropriate scan.</p> <p>Set a budget appropriate for the scope and frequency. Full-repository scans can take longer and cost more than diff scans. Treat <code>--max-cost</code> as an estimated cost limit, not a hard spending cap. Reaching it can leave coverage incomplete.</p> <ol> <li>Run the pipeline and review the results</li> </ol> <p>Submit the pipeline change through your normal review process, then trigger a scan. Confirm the target revision and scope in the run and <code>scan-manifest.json</code>.</p> <p>Review the findings and supporting evidence in the saved reports. Check <code>coverage.json</code> for incomplete or deferred areas, even if the scan reported no findings. Review runtime and cost before increasing the frequency or expanding to more repositories.</p> <p>Preserve reports as CI artifacts. Keep artifact access and retention appropriate for the source code and evidence they contain.</p> <p>Optionally export SARIF, a structured format for security findings, to display results in your platform's security interface. Check the platform guide for supported versions, permissions, and licensing requirements.</p> <ol> <li>Choose whether findings should block merging</li> </ol> <p>Start by reviewing findings without blocking merges. Once your team is comfortable with the results, you can require pull requests to pass a security check—for example, blocking merges when the scan finds a high- or critical-severity vulnerability.</p> <p>Always check whether the scan completed and what code it covered. A scan that failed or skipped code needs attention, even if it reported no findings.</p> <p>For setup details, see <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci#choose-a-severity-policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Configure severity thresholds and interpret scan results</a> (official section, online) <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/security/cli/ci\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Local page (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <ol> <li>Follow up on findings</li> </ol> <p>Assign findings for investigation or remediation through your team's normal process. Include the scanned commit, affected code, and supporting evidence so another developer can investigate.</p> <p>Verify fixes before closing findings, and address incomplete coverage in a follow-up scan.</p>"};
